---
// CommandCentreDim.astro — the closing CTA's dimmed Command Centre
// composition (spec §5, content brief §4's layout re-authored, its four
// numbered callouts dropped per the P0-gate decision in BUILD_FLAGS.md).
//
// Single-hue by construction: every fill and stroke below is `jade-lift` or
// `hairline` — no `accent`, `amber`, or `red` appears anywhere in this file.
// PLAN.md §3's correction to the literal spec reading: applying 25% opacity
// to a composition that DOES contain RAG colours leaves the coloured dots
// as bright specks while the near-black cards disappear, handing back
// exactly the data this composition is supposed to withhold. Single-hue
// first, then `opacity-dim` on the group, is what actually delivers
// "legible as a shape, unreadable as data."
//
// No <text> anywhere: this sidesteps two problems at once — Arabic text
// overflow in a fixed-width panel (PLAN.md §4 ambiguity 22, unsolved by the
// prototype) never arises, and "unreadable as data" is true by construction
// rather than by squinting at dimmed labels. Geometry only: rects and
// strokes standing in for the top bar, the sidebar's four phase groups, the
// three metric cards, the initiative table, the AI panel, and the benefit
// strip — proportions taken from the prototype's 900×520 (PLAN.md §4
// ambiguity 22), re-authored at a wider aspect so the composition reads as
// "a wide board" at full bleed, per PLAN.md §3.
//
// The gap between the table/AI-panel row and the benefit strip (y 402–480)
// is deliberately empty — nothing is drawn there. That hole is where
// ClosingCta.astro overlays the CTA text, per spec §5's own suggestion:
// designing the hole is the only way to get AA contrast without a scrim,
// and a scrim would be a card by another name.
//
// `aria-hidden`, not `role="img"` (PLAN.md §3's accessibility section): an
// honest `aria-label` for this composition would read the withheld Command
// Centre layout aloud, handing away the one thing the home page holds back.
// It is decorative by intent.
//
// RTL (P5): no lang prop needed — this fragment carries zero `<text>`
// (see above), so unlike StageGateQueue.astro a whole-group mirror is
// legitimate here (build task's own instruction: "CommandCentreDim has
// zero <text>, so a group mirror IS legitimate there if needed"). A plain
// CSS `scaleX(-1)` on the svg under `[dir="rtl"]` flips the sidebar to the
// inline-end edge and every card/table/strip along with it, with no risk of
// mirroring glyphs backwards because there are none to mirror. The
// block-direction fade mask below is applied to the *wrapping* div, not the
// svg, so the horizontal flip doesn't touch it.
---

<div class="command-centre-dim relative w-full">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 1600 640" class="block w-full" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    <g class="opacity-dim">
      <!-- top bar -->
      <rect x="0" y="0" width="1600" height="44" class="fill-jade-lift"></rect>

      <!-- sidebar, four phase groups -->
      <rect x="0" y="44" width="220" height="596" class="fill-jade-lift"></rect>
      {
        [76, 150, 250, 340].map((groupY) => (
          <>
            <rect x="30" y={groupY} width="160" height="10" rx="2" class="fill-hairline" />
            <rect x="30" y={groupY + 18} width="140" height="6" rx="2" class="fill-hairline" />
            <rect x="30" y={groupY + 32} width="120" height="6" rx="2" class="fill-hairline" />
          </>
        ))
      }

      <!-- three metric cards -->
      {
        [260, 660, 1060].map((cardX) => (
          <>
            <rect
              x={cardX}
              y="68"
              width="380"
              height="110"
              rx="4"
              class="fill-jade-lift stroke-hairline"
              stroke-width="1"
            />
            <rect x={cardX + 24} y="140" width={332} height="8" rx="2" class="fill-hairline" />
          </>
        ))
      }

      <!-- initiative table -->
      <rect
        x="260"
        y="202"
        width="760"
        height="200"
        rx="4"
        class="fill-jade-lift stroke-hairline"
        stroke-width="1"
      ></rect>
      {
        [0, 1, 2, 3, 4].map((row) => (
          <>
            <line
              x1="284"
              y1={242 + row * 32}
              x2="996"
              y2={242 + row * 32}
              class="stroke-hairline"
              stroke-width="1"
            />
            <rect
              x="700"
              y={228 + row * 32}
              width={90 + ((row * 37) % 130)}
              height="6"
              rx="2"
              class="fill-hairline"
            />
          </>
        ))
      }

      <!-- AI panel -->
      <rect
        x="1040"
        y="202"
        width="300"
        height="200"
        rx="4"
        class="fill-jade-lift stroke-hairline"
        stroke-width="1"
      ></rect>
      <rect x="1064" y="228" width="140" height="8" rx="2" class="fill-hairline"></rect>
      <rect x="1064" y="252" width="200" height="6" rx="2" class="fill-hairline"></rect>
      <rect x="1064" y="270" width="170" height="6" rx="2" class="fill-hairline"></rect>
      <rect x="1064" y="356" width="70" height="20" rx="2" class="stroke-hairline" fill="none" stroke-width="1"></rect>
      <rect x="1148" y="356" width="70" height="20" rx="2" class="stroke-hairline" fill="none" stroke-width="1"></rect>

      <!-- empty band, y 402–480: intentionally bare — the CTA text sits here -->

      <!-- benefit strip -->
      <rect
        x="260"
        y="480"
        width="1100"
        height="116"
        rx="4"
        class="fill-jade-lift stroke-hairline"
        stroke-width="1"
      ></rect>
      <polyline
        points="292,566 400,548 508,554 616,528 724,534 832,510 940,516 1048,494 1156,500 1264,478"
        fill="none"
        class="stroke-hairline"
        stroke-width="2"
      ></polyline>
      <polyline
        points="1264,478 1320,470"
        fill="none"
        class="stroke-hairline"
        stroke-width="2"
        stroke-dasharray="4 5"
      ></polyline>
      <line
        x1="1264"
        y1="486"
        x2="1264"
        y2="590"
        class="stroke-hairline"
        stroke-width="1"
        stroke-dasharray="2 4"
      ></line>
    </g>
  </svg>
</div>

<style>
  /* Fades the composition's block edges into the page ground (spec §5: "a
     mask that fades to the page ground"). Vertical only — top/bottom are
     unaffected by RTL, so this needs no direction-guarded variant. */
  .command-centre-dim {
    mask-image: linear-gradient(
      to bottom,
      transparent,
      black 14%,
      black 86%,
      transparent
    );
  }

  /* :global() around the ancestor selector: found alongside the identical
     SuggestionCard.astro bug at P5 — without it, Astro's scoped-style
     processor hashes `[dir="rtl"]` too, producing
     `[data-astro-cid-xxxxx][dir=rtl] ...`, which can never match because
     `dir="rtl"` lives on `<html>`, outside this component's scope. See
     SuggestionCard.astro's own comment and known-issues.md for the full
     explanation — same root cause, fixed the same way. */
  :global([dir="rtl"]) .command-centre-dim svg {
    transform: scaleX(-1);
  }
</style>
